#: ../../source/fun_project/02-fun_Gas_leak_alarm.rst:52
msgid "3. Code explanation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/02-fun_Gas_leak_alarm.rst:54
msgid "The core principle of the project revolves around continuously monitoring the gas concentration. When the detected gas concentration surpasses a certain threshold, it sets off an alarm and changes the LED's color to red. This serves as a simulated warning mechanism, indicative of potentially hazardous conditions. If the concentration drops below the threshold, the alarm is deactivated and the LED switches to green, indicating a safe environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/02-fun_Gas_leak_alarm.rst:56
msgid "Defining Constants and Variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/02-fun_Gas_leak_alarm.rst:58
msgid "These lines declare and initialize the pin numbers for various components. The ``sensorPin`` denotes the analog pin where the MQ-2 gas sensor is connected. ``sensorValue`` is an integer variable storing the sensor's analog output. The ``buzzerPin`` indicates the digital pin to which the buzzer is connected. Finally, the ``RPin`` and ``GPin`` are the pins for the red and green channels of the RGB LED, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/02-fun_Gas_leak_alarm.rst:74
msgid "Initialization in ``setup()``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/02-fun_Gas_leak_alarm.rst:76
msgid "The ``setup()`` function initializes the required settings. Serial communication begins at a baud rate of 9600, allowing us to view sensor readings on the Serial Monitor. Pins for the buzzer and RGB LED are set as ``OUTPUT``, meaning they'll send signals out to external components."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/02-fun_Gas_leak_alarm.rst:90
msgid "Main Loop: Reading Sensor and Triggering Alarm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/02-fun_Gas_leak_alarm.rst:92
msgid "The ``loop()`` function continually reads the gas sensor's output. The reading is then displayed on the Serial Monitor for observation. Depending on the sensor value, two scenarios can occur:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/02-fun_Gas_leak_alarm.rst:94
msgid "If the value exceeds 300, the buzzer is activated using ``tone()``, and the RGB LED turns red."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/02-fun_Gas_leak_alarm.rst:95
msgid "If the value is below 300, the buzzer is silenced using ``noTone()``, and the LED turns green."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/02-fun_Gas_leak_alarm.rst:97
msgid "Lastly, a delay of 50 milliseconds is introduced before the next loop iteration to manage the read frequency and reduce the CPU load."
msgstr ""
